Recorded voltage: 12.08 V DC

Conclusion: The measured voltage is above 11.5 V, so this test does not indicate an obvious low-voltage 12 V rail problem.

If the reading were below 11.5 V, it could indicate a failing or weak PSU/SMPS, particularly a problem with its 12 V output. This can cause random shutdowns, especially when the PC is under load.
